  <running_head>MATERIARUM.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="2">1. Surdus &amp; mutus adhibitâ distinctione te-</l>
    <l n="3">stantur.</l>
    <l n="4">2. Moribus res aliter sese habet.</l>
    <l n="5">3. Quid jure Canonum?</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="7">1. Caci testamentum est mixti generis.</l>
    <l n="8">2. Mores tantum ordinarias solemnitates</l>
    <l n="9">desiderant.</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="11">1. Ab hostibus capti testari nequeunt.</l>
    <l n="12">2. In civitate quod factum erat testamen-</l>
    <l n="13">tum, sustinetur.</l>
    <l n="14">3. Quodnam tempus spectandum, ut te-</l>
    <l n="15">stator habilis fuisse dicatur?</l>
    <l n="16">4. Quis locus inspiciendus circa conditio-</l>
    <l n="17">nem testatoris?</l>
    <l n="18">5. Cujus loci habenda ratio in ordine ad</l>
    <l n="19">testamenti solemnia.</l>
    <l n="20">6. Mores sustinent eorum testamenta, qui</l>
    <l n="21">apud hostes testati fuerint.</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT.13.</l>
    <l n="23">1. TESTAMENTUM patris inter liberos</l>
    <l n="24">est plus quam solemne.</l>
    <l n="25">2. Institutio &amp; exheredatio describitur.</l>
    <l n="26">3. Differentia inter filium &amp; filiam circa</l>
    <l n="27">exheredationem.</l>
    <l n="28">4. Praeteritio definitur.</l>
    <l n="29">5. Filio in potestate praeterito testamentum</l>
    <l n="30">est nullum.</l>
    <l n="31">6. Secus obtinet in filiâ praeteritâ.</l>
    <l n="32" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="33">1. Posthumus praeteritus rumpit testamen-</l>
    <l n="34">tum.</l>
    <l n="35">2. Differentia servata inter posthumum &amp;</l>
    <l n="36">posthumam.</l>
    <l n="37" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="38">1. Posthumi sunt vel veri, vel quasi.</l>
    <l n="39">2. Quae formula circa posthumos inventa?</l>
    <l n="40" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">Liberi emancipati praeteriti non dicunt</l>
    <l n="42">testamentum nullum.</l>
    <l n="43" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">Adoptivi impune poterunt praeteriri.</l>
    <l n="45" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="46">
      <i>Jus novissimum proponitur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="47" para="true">
      <i>§. 6.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="48" para="true">
      <i>Miles potest liberos praeterire.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="49" para="true">
      <i>§. 7.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="50" para="true">1. <i>Mater &amp; avus maternus idem potest.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="51" para="true">2. <i>Quid obtineat jure Hebræorum ?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="52" para="true">3. <i>Quid moribus?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="53" type="heading" level="1" caput="14" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT. 14.</l>
    <l n="54" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Hæredibus instituendis.</l>
    <l n="55" para="true">1. <i>HÆredis institutio est fundam-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="56">
      <i>entum testamenti.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="57" para="true">2. <i>Et absolute facta eam quæ obliqua est,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="58">
      <i>vel verbis facta precariis excludit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="59" para="true">3. <i>Hæredis institutio de persona in perso-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="60">
      <i>nam extenditur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="61" para="true">4. <i>Quandoque de casu in casum extenditur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="62" para="true">5. <i>Positi in conditione non sunt vocati ex</i>
    </l>
    <l n="63">
      <i>testamento.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="64" para="true">6. <i>Quidam institui non possunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="65" para="true">7. <i>Quidam in partem aliquam admit-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="66">
      <i>tuntur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="67" para="true">8. <i>Quidem absolute institui poterunt, ut servi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="68" para="true">9. <i>Qui servi dicantur proprii ?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="69" para="true">10. <i>Exceptio proponitur a regulâ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="70" para="true">
      <i>§. 1.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
